course: dictionary
lesson: 2834
title: Words about families
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «The divorce came through» is about the law: the court has finished the legal ending of a marriage.
explain: A divorce is the official legal end of a marriage, so the husband and wife are no longer married. As a verb, divorce means to end a marriage by law. Formally, it can also mean to separate two things completely, as in "you can't divorce sport from fun".
explain: Families can still love and care for children after a divorce. Divorce is never a child's fault. If you feel sad, angry or worried, that is normal, and it helps to talk to someone you trust.
fact: A divorce is the legal ending of a marriage.
fact: «Divorced» is an adjective: in «divorced parents», it tells you the parents are no longer married.
fact: A solicitor is a kind of lawyer who helps with legal things like a divorce. Seeing one does not mean anyone is in trouble with the police.
fact: A divorce is never a child's fault.
fact: When parents are «splitting up», they are separating or divorcing, and a child can feel ill from the worry.
exercise: «A divorce is the official legal end of a marriage.» What is a divorce? | A holiday that a family takes together | A party for two married people | *The legal ending of a marriage | A kind of school trip
exercise: Sam tells his sister that Jake's parents are «divorcing». What does divorcing mean here? | Having a big party | Going on holiday together | Moving house to a new town | *Ending their marriage by law
exercise: What is a solicitor? | A teacher who teaches law at school | A judge who lives in a court | *A kind of lawyer who helps with legal things like a divorce | A police officer who visits families
test: What is true about divorce and children? | Children should keep divorce secret | Children cannot feel sad about divorce | Divorce is always the child's fault | *Divorce is never a child's fault
test: In «divorced parents», which word tells us about the parents? | family | parents | children | *divorced
exam: What should a child do if they feel sad or angry after a divorce? | Stop talking to everyone they know | Keep it secret for a year | Blame themselves for it | *Talk to someone they trust
